<%#
  views/partials/sidebar.ejs

  The sidebar of the public pages, with the weather widget (requirements: a weather
  widget in the site's sidebar, from an external web service).

  The widget arrives with "Loading weather..." and is filled in the browser by
  public/js/public/weatherWidget.js from our own GET /api/weather. Why not render the
  weather on the server with the page: the feed and article pages would then wait for the
  weather before they could be sent, and a slow weather service would slow down the whole
  site. Loading it separately keeps the article text fast, and the widget refreshes itself
  while the page stays open (every 5 minutes, see weatherWidget.js).

  The page that includes this partial must also load /js/shared/apiClient.js and then
  /js/public/weatherWidget.js at the end of its body.

  aside is the semantic HTML5 element for content beside the main content; on a narrow
  screen the CSS moves it below the main content (public/css/main.css).

  Included by: views/public/feed.ejs and views/public/article.ejs.
  Owner: SH.
%>
<aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Sidebar">
    <section id="weather-widget" class="card loading" aria-labelledby="weather-title">
        <h3 id="weather-title">Weather</h3>
        <%# aria-live="polite": screen readers announce the weather when it arrives or changes. %>
        <div id="weather-content" aria-live="polite">Loading weather...</div>
    </section>
</aside>
